Method Overriding
-----------------
The process if inheriting the method and changing the implemention of inherited method is called method overriding.
IS-A Relationship is mandatory.

In order to achive method overriding we will have to follow the following rules.
  1 method name must be same
  2 parameter should be same.
  3 return type should be same
  4 access modifier should be same or of higher visibility.

@Override
It is the annotation in java which is used to check the correctness of the overriden method.
Without the anotation also te program works and execute successfully but it is highly recomended to use in thr program.
It was introduced in JDK 1.5


